                                        "entry_id": "a943b751-ab3b-36ab-9664-8f4f7f61761e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Son of Aeolus and Enarete, and king of Ephyra, as tragic figure doomed eternally to roll a boulder up a hill in Tartarus, a part of Hades."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Greek"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ec005cc0-493d-4d65-a539-edf232e82697",
                                                "sense_id": "65d28f08-6362-308c-90be-cfdfa6592ecf",
                                                "text": "Indeed, I have looked upon the fable of Sisyphus as an allegory, and that his wife was the stone which so perpetually rolled back upon his hands, effectually retarding his weary progress up-hill."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
